"about.menu" = "About LiveCore Studio";
"about.version" = "Version %@";
"about.text" = "LiveCore Studio is a native macOS live production studio: switch cameras, capture cards, videos, titles and web pages, mix audio, then record, stream to several platforms at once and send the program to screens or NDI. Built for events, weddings, churches, classrooms and talk shows that need a fast, stable and simple studio on a Mac.";
"about.made_by" = "Made by Munawar Tamimi";
"help.menu" = "LiveCore Studio Help";
"help.title" = "Help";
"help.search" = "Search help";
"help.footer" = "This help describes LiveCore Studio 0.48. Features still in testing are marked in docs/FEATURE_STATUS.md.";
"help.start.title" = "Getting started";
"help.start.body" = "LiveCore Studio works like a vision mixer: inputs on the left, Preview and Program in the middle, audio and outputs at the bottom.\n## First show in five steps\n• Start a new project or pick a template (File › New from Template).\n• Add inputs with the + button above the input list.\n• Click an input to put it in Preview, then press CUT or AUTO to send it to Program.\n• Check the audio meters in the mixer.\n• Press RECORD or STREAM in the bottom bar.\n## Saving\n• ⌘S saves the project (inputs, layouts, titles, audio, outputs). Stream keys stay in the macOS Keychain, never in the project file.\n• Autosave keeps a recovery copy; after a crash LiveCore offers to restore it.";
"help.inputs.title" = "Inputs";
"help.inputs.body" = "## Adding inputs (+ button)\n• Camera › Video Capture: webcams, UVC capture cards (e.g. Datavideo CAP 2), iPhone (Continuity Camera). Pick the device, format and audio in the sheet.\n• Media: video, video playlist, image, photo slideshow, presentation (PDF / Keynote export).\n• Graphics: titles and lower thirds (Title Designer), timers, frames, GT titles, subtitles, scenes.\n• Other: browser (web page), screen capture, NDI, colour bars, solid colours.\n## Working with inputs\n• Right-click an input for Preview, Cut direct, lock, rename, properties and colour.\n• Properties (gear) has tabs: Source, Colour, Key (chroma key), AI and PTZ where the input supports them.\n• Playlist: drag a clip up or down to reorder. Loop is off by default for new playlists.\n• Browser: Edit opens the page in its own window to log in or click; Done puts it back. The page is not reloaded between edits.";
"help.switching.title" = "Switching";
"help.switching.body" = "• Preview (left) is what goes on air next; Program (right) is on air.\n• CUT switches instantly, AUTO plays the selected transition (fade, wipe, slide, stinger…). Drag the T-bar for a manual transition.\n• Keyboard shortcuts are empty at first: pick a preset or set your own keys in Settings › Keyboard shortcuts.\n• Multiview (grid icon in the top bar) opens a window with all inputs, Preview and Program for a second screen.";
"help.overlays.title" = "Overlays and titles";
"help.overlays.body" = "• Four overlay channels put titles, logos or picture-in-picture above Program.\n• The numbered overlay buttons on an input tile: click puts the overlay in Preview, right-click (two-finger click) takes it straight to Program.\n• Title Designer: text, shapes, images and animations, with templates for news, sport, church, wedding and talk shows.\n• Titles can read live data from CSV files or links.";
"help.audio.title" = "Audio mixer";
"help.audio.body" = "• Every input with sound gets a channel strip: fader, mute, solo, gain, EQ, compressor and noise gate.\n• Master goes to recording and stream. The limiter protects against clipping.\n• AUX / BUS: use the + menu in the mixer to add up to four buses (A–D) and send channels to them, e.g. for a hall PA, a recorder or mix-minus for a remote guest.\n• Loudness meter (LUFS) helps keep streams at a steady level.\n• Online radio and music playlists can be added as audio inputs (HTTPS stations only).";
"help.record.title" = "Recording, MultiCorder and replay";
"help.record.body" = "• RECORD records Program with the master audio. The gear next to it sets format, quality and folder.\n• MULTICORDER records chosen inputs as separate clean files (ISO) for editing later.\n• Snapshot saves a still of Program.\n• Instant replay keeps the last seconds of Program; play them back at normal or slow speed.\n• A blinking NOT RECORDING badge over Program reminds you when nothing is recording (Settings can turn it off).";
"help.stream.title" = "Streaming";
"help.stream.body" = "• STREAM sends Program to one or more destinations at once: YouTube, Facebook, Twitch, or any RTMP / RTMPS server.\n• Stream keys are stored only in the macOS Keychain.\n• Each destination shows its status, bitrate and reconnects; LiveCore reconnects automatically after a network drop.\n• 9:16 (top bar) makes a vertical version of the show for Reels, Shorts and TikTok, with its own stream.\n• The padlock in the bottom bar locks RECORD and STREAM so they cannot be stopped by accident.";
"help.outputs.title" = "Outputs";
"help.outputs.body" = "Open the OUTPUTS panel from the top bar (⇧⌘O).\n## FULLSCREEN\n• Shows Program (or another source) full screen on a second display or projector. ⇧⌘F toggles it.\n## EXTERNAL\n• NDI: send Program over the network; with NDI Virtual Camera it becomes a webcam for Zoom, Teams or Meet.";
"help.color.title" = "Colour and LUTs";
"help.color.body" = "Open an input's properties › Colour.\n• Brightness, contrast, saturation and gamma; flip and rotate.\n• Video levels: capture cards that look grey or washed out are corrected automatically; you can also set the range by hand.\n## LUT\n• Load .cube: use any 3D LUT (Resolve, Premiere, camera LUTs). A copy is kept in the LiveCore LUT library.\n• Strength mixes the LUT with the original picture.\n• LUT Generator: start from a preset (Warm Wedding, Teal & Orange, Cinematic Film, B&W…) and adjust exposure, white balance, film contrast, lift / gamma / gain, vibrance, split toning, fade and highlight roll-off. The input shows the look live. Save & Apply stores it in the library; Export writes a .cube for other apps.";
"help.show.title" = "Show tools";
"help.show.body" = "• RUNDOWN (top bar): the running order of the event with timed segments; segments can move on automatically.\n• Highlights (⇧⌘H) mark moments during the show; the client package collects recordings, chapters and highlights.\n• Pre-flight check (⇧⌘P) tests disk space, devices, audio and frame rate before going live.\n• Templates set up a whole show (wedding, church, webinar, podcast…) in one step.";
"help.remote.title" = "Remote control";
"help.remote.body" = "• Web Controller: control LiveCore from a phone or tablet on the same network (Settings › Remote). Protect it with a PIN; the PIN is kept in the Keychain.\n• MIDI: map buttons and faders of a MIDI controller with Learn (Settings › MIDI).\n• Keyboard shortcuts can be changed in Settings › Shortcuts.";
"help.tips.title" = "Tips and troubleshooting";
"help.tips.body" = "• Frame drops: keep the output frame rate equal to your cameras (e.g. 30 or 25), close unused windows and prefer 1080p sources.\n• Capture card colours look grey: open Colour and check Video levels (automatic or limited › full).\n• A camera does not appear: unplug and plug it in again, then use Refresh in the Video Capture sheet. Allow camera and microphone access in System Settings › Privacy.\n• Streaming fails: check the stream key and your upload speed (about 1.5× the stream bitrate).\n• Help › Export Logs & Diagnostics makes a file you can send for support (without stream keys).";


